            <ArticleTitle>Hemorrhagic pseudocyst of the adrenal gland causing acute abdominal pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>379-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute abdominal pain is a common clinical entity with varied etiology. Hemorrhagic pseudocysts of the adrenal gland are rare lesions that might be considered in the differential diagnosis of acute abdominal pain. Herein, we report a case of young married female presenting with acute pain abdomen and fever, who was diagnosed to have hemorrhagic pseudocyst of the adrenal gland.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
